    "details": "# Problem Description:\n\nSeveral encoding modules, including HZ, UTF-7, VIQR, and ZW, did not\nproperly check the size of the caller-supplied output buffer before\nwriting converted characters. \\[CVE-2026-58081\\]\n\nThe ISO-2022 encoding module used a stack buffer sized to MB_LEN_MAX (6\nbytes) for intermediate character output. Some ISO-2022 variants can\nrequire up to 10 bytes per character, in which case conversions can\ntrigger a stack buffer overflow of up to four bytes. \\[CVE-2026-58082\\]\n\n# Impact:\n\nAn application that uses iconv(3) to convert untrusted input to or from\none of the affected encodings may be vulnerable to buffer overflows if\nit uses one of the affected encoding modules.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0316",
